    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d286">

                <pb facs="0661" n="635" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v03/pg635"/>

                <head>286. Message From the Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Vietnam(Lodge)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d286-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                ><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                                when="1963-08-25">August 25, 1963</date></hi>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Re CAS Saigon 0292.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d286-f2"/></p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Agree to modification proposed.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Re CAS Saigon 0291<anchor n="3" xml:id="d286-f3"/> reporting approach by
                        General Khanh. Our impression is that Khanh one of best of Generals, both
                        courageous and sophisticated. His analysis seems to confirm other evidence
                        indicating need for speed in making US position clear to Generals. Hope
                        review E and E plans can be accomplished quickly.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Re Deptel 244.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d286-f4"/> Press already aware general
                        picture from own sources, e.g. NY Times today says “reports from Saigon
                        indicate top Vietnamese Generals did approve plans for martial law, but not
                        for raids on Buddhist pagodas, shooting and widespread arrests carried out
                        by the special forces under Mr. Nhu’s control.” Will therefore proceed
                        background press along lines Deptel 244 this afternoon and VOA will
                        broadcast Monday morning Saigon time.</item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>Re CAS Saigon 0293.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d286-f5"/> Suggest Ambassador
                        decide best means getting word to Generals.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
